00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:23.740
So why not go all the way back to...

00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:25.980
Sorry, original Xbox ain't that retro.

00:27:26.900 --> 00:27:31.420
But why not go all the way back to the NES and play NES Tennis and see if that's any good?

00:27:31.620 --> 00:27:33.100
Well, why not just go back to Pong?

00:27:33.380 --> 00:27:34.440
Find out what that's like.

00:27:36.780 --> 00:27:38.880
So Sam, is this on your essential games list?

00:27:39.660 --> 00:27:42.900
Well, let me tell you, this is not on my essential games list.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:45.000
Is that breaking news? Yeah.

00:27:45.240 --> 00:27:47.440
Okay. Yeah. Breaking news.

00:27:47.580 --> 00:27:49.520
I would put Wii Sports Tennis.

00:27:49.780 --> 00:27:50.720
Like, way above it.

00:27:50.820 --> 00:27:55.060
I think that was like a much better representation of kind of like party tennis.

00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:56.900
Even though it's not like as difficult.

00:27:57.240 --> 00:27:59.700
Which I feel like this has an interesting curve to it.

00:27:59.900 --> 00:28:02.720
Again, we kind of have been saying this with sports games before.

00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:07.240
Where if you like tennis games or if you like tennis, this might be something to check out.

00:28:07.460 --> 00:28:10.400
Because it is interesting all the things they were able to do.

00:28:10.540 --> 00:28:13.940
Just with, you know, a directional pad and a button for swing.

00:28:14.120 --> 00:28:16.660
You know? The controls are kind of frustrating.

00:28:17.020 --> 00:28:18.960
I think the movement speed is a little bit annoying.

00:28:18.960 --> 00:28:20.840
So it's not on the list.

00:28:20.980 --> 00:28:22.480
And I'm just going to say something here.

00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:24.980
We've been saying that about some sports games.

00:28:25.300 --> 00:28:26.840
I'm not going to say that here with tennis.

00:28:27.140 --> 00:28:29.380
And it's not that I hate this game by any means.

00:28:29.580 --> 00:28:33.200
I just don't think that if you're a fan of tennis games, it's worth going back to this.

00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:36.120
I think that there's plenty of tennis going on.

00:28:36.940 --> 00:28:38.860
And that's kind of an interesting statement, too.

00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:40.700
Because as I mentioned earlier, there's not that many tennis games.

00:28:40.700 --> 00:28:46.940
But there's enough good tennis games out there that you don't have to play something as archaic as these older tennis games.

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:48.200
Pong is its own thing.

00:28:48.460 --> 00:28:49.860
You know? Like, Pong is different.

00:28:50.080 --> 00:28:53.760
That's just, that's like really abstract gaming at its finest, you know?

00:28:54.320 --> 00:28:57.660
This, on the other hand, that Z-axis, I can't get over it.

00:28:57.660 --> 00:29:01.160
The computers are just a little too challenging.

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:07.040
And the only thing that I'm really going to praise this game for is that it is a constant fight with the computer.

00:29:07.040 --> 00:29:10.600
That you never really have a sure hand in anything.

00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:13.680
If you're up three sets, that doesn't mean anything in this game.

00:29:13.860 --> 00:29:17.720
Mia, you've heard my spiel about sports games over and over.

00:29:17.980 --> 00:29:18.820
Sam said it.

00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:21.580
Mike said a version of it.

00:29:21.660 --> 00:29:26.560
There's no reason to play this game unless you have it in front of you.

00:29:26.560 --> 00:29:28.740
So, it's not on the essential games list.

00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:30.700
It is a very competent game.

00:29:30.920 --> 00:29:36.100
That's about it. Yeah, I think that it would take a lot for me to put this on my essential games list.

00:29:36.120 --> 00:29:37.620
It would take a lot more than what this game offers.

00:29:38.540 --> 00:29:47.480
But I think, like, the biggest thing that kind of jumps out at me is that it doesn't simulate aiming in tennis as well enough.

00:29:47.480 --> 00:29:51.620
And that's kind of like a big thing that stops it from feeling as intuitive as it should.

00:29:51.760 --> 00:29:54.540
Otherwise, the controls work pretty well, but definitely not essential.

00:29:54.540 --> 00:29:59.740
Yeah, I think one thing you carried out there, Joe, is that, like, it's a little difficult because it's unintuitive.

00:29:59.940 --> 00:30:02.300
It's not difficult just for the sake of difficulty.

00:30:02.540 --> 00:30:11.500
It's actually, like, you know, the aiming and, like, the generosity of, like, your timing in other tennis games is there for a good reason.

00:30:11.500 --> 00:30:14.480
Mm-hmm. So, that's how I feel about tennis.

00:30:14.800 --> 00:30:19.780
Again, you know, our essential games list should be small and fine-tuned.

00:30:19.980 --> 00:30:26.940
And I just don't think, you know, we've now finished all the sports games and none of them, the NES launched sports games.

00:30:27.140 --> 00:30:29.120
There's plenty more sports games to come.

00:30:29.620 --> 00:30:31.520
And none of them made the essential games list.

00:30:31.520 --> 00:30:40.440
It doesn't mean that a sports game won't ever make our essential games list, but certainly these earlier versions have a lot to work on if they want to enter our essential games list.

00:30:40.620 --> 00:30:45.100
Any other thoughts? Yeah, I would just say that I think this game goes in the jank folder.

00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:48.040
Nice. Yeah. The jank folder back.

00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:57.160
Yeah. I think that we could make at least a segment of another Twitch stream out of this game because it is so, oh, no, we can't play against each other.

00:30:57.360 --> 00:30:59.580
Right. Can't play against each other, but we can watch.

00:30:59.580 --> 00:31:00.520
The sunburned people.

00:31:00.720 --> 00:31:11.400
Yeah. The other three of us could just, like, pray for the person who's playing, you know, like call Roger Federer and ask him, you know, as a tennis god, can you help us out here?

00:31:11.740 --> 00:31:14.600
And he'd be like, oh, wait, the one for the NES?

00:31:14.900 --> 00:31:16.500
Oh, no. Oh, no, yeah.

00:31:16.960 --> 00:31:19.560
You don't want me. You're not up against a sunburned guy, are you?

00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:22.640
He has nightmares about that guy.

00:31:23.420 --> 00:31:24.540
All right. That's us.

